  "notes": "Philadelphia's rawest neo-soul voice, tracked with the Roots' band and the A Touch of Jazz board. `confidence` is **low** because the research rates the entry medium-low: the era, the label and the production milieu are sourced, but it says plainly that \"the parametric detail is Philadelphia-lane inference and marked\". What is stated drives the drums — \"Questlove-school live kit — snare late and heavy, kick early, swung 16th hats, tambourine on the backbeat, and stop-time hits before the chorus\" — so the snare displacement is 10–20 ms at a high ghost velocity, the tambourine mirrors the clap, and `fillBeforeSection` is on for the stop-time. The band is the stated 70–98. Harmony is \"i–iv–V with a raised 7th on the dominant, gospel passing chords, and blues-third melodic clashes against minor harmony\", which is why harmonic minor sits in the scale set, `susOrDimProb` is raised for the passing chords, and `halfStepDissonance` is the highest in this batch for the blues third. Melody is \"low, gritty, shouted at the top of the range, with heavy blues ornament and speech breaking into the line — very high dynamic range within a phrase\", encoded as a wide register with a call-and-response structure rather than as pitch content. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are every drum and melody number, and the second progression family: the entry writes i–iv–V, and the shortened i–iv is this author's reading of the same cadence rather than a numeral the research gave.",
